{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And they shall stumble, one against another.</b> When they run to flee, they will stumble over one another — because they will rush to run." "<b>As if from the sword.</b> As though fleeing from killers — there will be panic in their hearts, and at every moment they imagine a man is pursuing them. And its midrash: וְכָשְׁלוּ אִישׁ בְּאָחִיו — this one stumbles through the sin of that one, for all Israel are guarantors for one another (Sifra; Sanhedrin 27)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:48.394396288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}